PROTOCOL="# EURCHF M15 LONG Pass3 — bounded frequency recovery\n\nPredeclared 9 October 2026, following the AUDJPY 2026-09-24 template as a guide.\nRead-only research; full frozen history remains reused exploratory/in-sample.\n\n## Fixed history and execution\nKeep SAME EURCHF_M15_PASS1_FROZEN_DATA.zip next to research app.py.\n546647 native OANDA MID M15 /137939 H1 observations. Requested2005-01-01 to\n2026-10-08T00Z exclusive; actual first2005-01-02T18:45Z,last2026-10-07T23:45Z.\nNo fetching, missing-day synthesis, era/calendar removal or extra credentials.\nExact bullish engulf, ATR14 seeded TR1..14 then Wilder/current causal ATR;\ncommon warmup200; prior low excludes signal. Structure frozen within anchors:\noriginal lookback200/absolute low-distance<=.05ATR; tight lookback100/<=.025ATR.\nStop signalLow-1pip; reference signalClose; RR3 target from reference-stop.\nBUY assumed adverse entry costs10/20/40ticks=1/2/4pips; risk denominator fill-stop.\nPrimary STOP_FIRST_GAP_STRESS includes adverse stop gaps/capped target gaps and\nstop-first dual touch. Alternate NEAREST_OPEN_SENSITIVITY retains exact prior\nnearest-extreme/tie-stop/barrier prices. Per-case full P0 replay; exit-candle\nentry eligible, invalid geometry does not occupy, unresolved positions occupy\nthrough cutoff and have no invented R. Entries [start,end); exits (start,end].\n\n## Only new research question\nCan modestly weaker body/range requirements improve activity without losing\ncost/window/temporal support, in the already observed H1 volatility context?\nFreeze latest completed native H1 ATR14 / mean exactly200 preceding ATRs >=1.00.\nTested H1 ATR excluded from its mean; require all200 values available. Latest\nH1 close<=signal entry. No M15/daily filter stacking or context-age filter.\nBody minima1.00/1.25ATR x range minima1.25/1.50ATR x two anchor geometries.\nEight research definitions: two exact existing filtered IDs plus six new ones.\nSix new unfiltered geometry controls and six same-geometry H1-availability\ncontrols separate body/range effects from availability/volatility filtering.\nEvery59 prior Pass2B definition retained exactly: 57 now labelled CONTROL,\ntwo are research controls. Total77definitions/462execution-cost cases. Original\nM15/H1 window100/200/300,floors.75/1/1.25 and separate daily comparators remain\nfixed diagnostics, not an expanded search. All354 archived cases must retain\nraw-signal hashes and canonical full accepted-ledger hashes/counts before new\noutcomes. Controls:69 definitions,59 archived,22 availability,4 daily diagnostics.\n\n## Evidence, activity and comparisons\nAll full source/context/features/masks/paths/accepted/invalid/open ledgers,\nisolated-vs-P0,35periods/262months/714rolling windows per case including zeros,\nblank years/months/droughts/cost-stop buckets/equivalences exported unchanged.\nEvery research row has matched same-geometry availability and old filtered\nsame-anchor frequency reference. frequency_recovery_comparisons.csv reports\ncommon/added/removed entries and R plus count/blank/DD changes against the old\nfiltered anchor. frequency_recovery_periods.csv exposes those changes for all\n35 periods, including latest1/2/3/5/10Y. frequency_recovery_entry_differences.csv\njoins changed accepted trades with their full execution fields and raw flags.\nAdditions/removals are actual independent full replay differences; loosening\ncan displace old trades. Replaying additions in isolation is not portfolio R.\nBody/range neighbours vary ONE axis only within the same anchor; anchor changes\nare not neighbours. Duplicate fingerprints are not independent support.\n\n## Decision guide\nJudge all eight settings and both anchor families, two/four-pip costs and both\nexit assumptions. Seek useful additional recent activity, positive marginal\naccepted R, reasonable older-era/rolling loss and a coherent neighbouring region.\nMore signals/highest lifetime R alone are insufficient. Keep weak/zero eras and\npartial2026/October explicit. No automatic winner or promises of recovery.\nIf added activity loses, costs fail, support is isolated or recent activity is\nstill negligible, park this route instead of stacking rescue filters. A supported\nrelaxed region later needs its OWN window100/300 confirmation; old geometry's\nwindow support does not transfer automatically. No RR sweep or entry-price tuning.\nNo untouched OOS claim. MID+assumed adverse entry omits executable bid/ask and\nfinancing. Closed additiveR/DD is not NAV%, marked equity or a gap-loss bound.\nLive Portfolio32/EURCHF H1 SHORT unchanged; no broker calls, execution orders,\nportfolio admission, live deployment or activation changes.\n"
